    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0690" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg630"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Señor Lerdo de Tejada to Mr. Plumb.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-11-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 27, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir</hi>: I have received the copies which
                    you have been pleased to send to me unofficially with your letter of to-day of
                    the note addressed to you by the Hon. Secretary of State of the United States,
                    and of the note annexed of the Hon. Secretary of the Treasury, upon the subject
                    of the free zone on the Rio Grande frontier, with reference to which we
                    conferred in our interviews of the 6th and 25th instant.</p>
                <p>As I had the pleasure to state to you in those interviews, the government has
                    been occupied, and will continue to give its attention to this matter with the
                    serious consideration that it merits.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>S. LERDO DE TEJADA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward Lee Plumb</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
